## mod-compared Progression (all 10 captured heartbeats)
  T=6343 mod-compared=42845
  T=6463 mod-compared=45125  (+2280)
  T=6583 mod-compared=47405  (+2280)
  T=6703 mod-compared=49685  (+2280)
  T=6823 mod-compared=51965  (+2280)
  T=6943 mod-compared=54245  (+2280)
  T=7063 mod-compared=56525  (+2280)
  T=7183 mod-compared=58805  (+2280)
  T=7303 mod-compared=61085  (+2280)
  T=7423 mod-compared=63365  (+2280)

  Monotonic +2280 per heartbeat. active-ticks increments +120 per
  heartbeat. Ratio mod-compared / active-ticks ≈ 19:1.

  **This ratio is the V5 signature**: CLIENT runs FishNet
  reconcile-replay. Each forward physics tick on CLIENT triggers
  N replay RunInputs (replay window size) + 1 forward RunInputs.
  `_shadowModifierConsumedCount` increments inside RunInputs
  (motor.cs:362) on every call — forward AND replay. `_shadowActiveCompares`
  increments inside Shadow_CompareAndReport (OnPostTick) which
  fires once per FORWARD tick only. Observed ratio of 19 implies
  replay window averaging 18 ticks (~300ms of rollback), consistent
  with Steam lobby RTT + FishNet prediction buffer.

  **This is exactly the distinct state-source that V5 is designed
  to exercise** (audit §4): replay Resolve runs on reconcile-sourced
  _modifierState (overwritten at motor.cs:471), forward Resolve runs
  on post-consume _modifierState. Zero mod-div across all captured
  heartbeats confirms bit-identical Resolve output in both paths —
  and, crucially, confirms no serializer-precision drift between
  server's serialized ComputedStats and client's locally-re-resolved
  ComputedStats (the Phase 8 cleanup-queue Entry 1 watchpoint).

